WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.600
Tessl is the package manager for skills and context. Skills are a powerful tool for steering

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.200
agent behavior, expanding on things like editing your agents.md or adding documentation. But

3
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.400
managing skills requires more than just copying words around. You need to think about how do you

4
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:22.080
own them over time? Are they effective? And which skills do you choose in the first place? If you

5
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.680
are consuming skills, Tessl helps you install any skill and keeps a record in a tessl.json

6
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.760
file that remembers which skills are installed and helps you update them and manage them over

7
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:39.200
time. It includes evaluation for every skill that you consume, which lets you choose which one is

8
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.480
correct and which one is not. And it seamlessly installs them for all the agents you have without

9
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.360
duplicating content inside your repository. If you are producing skills of your own,

10
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.000
Tessl helps you evaluate and optimize them, making sure your skills are as good as they

11
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.640
can be. It then helps you publish and version them so users can know what they are using and

12
00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.800
make sure they're always on the latest and greatest. Finally, it helps you keep skills

13
00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.160
fresh by tracking related software changes and updating your skill if needed. This ensures that

14
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:14.320
your skill doesn't go stale and misguide agents. Skills and context are more than just words. They

15
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.840
are the unit of software in the world of agentic development. Tessl is a developer

16
00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:24.000
grade package manager for skills and context and the development platform for managing context in

17
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.200
your organization. Making sure your agents get the right context at the right time. Get started

18
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:36.720
for free at tessl.io/registry or contact us if you want to try within your organization.
